<%# Saved, as a shelf rather than a river (D-reader-density).

    Unread is chronological triage: newest first, one line each, get through
    it. Saved is the opposite kind of thing — a small collection you come
    back to, where the question is "which one was that" rather than "what's
    next". Same data, different shape: cards, and ordered by when *you* kept
    it rather than when the world published it, because that is the order
    you will remember it in.

    No images, deliberately. The obvious way to make this look good is to
    render the publisher's own <media:content>, but an <img> pointing at
    their CDN hands them the reader's IP and a timestamp for every article
    they've shown interest in — a per-article read receipt, sent from inside
    a signed-in session. That is exactly the leak OUTBOUND's `noreferrer`
    and the stripped entry HTML exist to prevent, so the shelf is
    typographic and the faces carry the identity. If images are ever wanted,
    the honest way is to proxy them through the app.

    Locals: page. %>
<div class="reader-shelf">
  <% page.items.each do |item| %>
    <% url = reader_safe_url(item.url) %>
    <article id="<%= dom_id(item) %>" class="reader-card group">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
        <%= feed_face(item.feed) %>
        <span class="min-w-0 flex-1 truncate text-xs text-soft"><%= reader_source(item.feed) %></span>
        <time class="shrink-0 text-xs tabular-nums text-soft"
              datetime="<%= item.saved_at&.iso8601 %>"
              title="Saved <%= l(item.saved_at, format: :long) if item.saved_at %>">
          <%= reader_age(item.saved_at) %>
        </time>
      </div>

      <h3 class="mt-2 line-clamp-3 text-sm font-semibold text-ink">
        <% if url %>
          <%= link_to item.title, url, class: "hover:underline", **ReaderHelper::OUTBOUND %>
        <% else %>
          <%= item.title %>
        <% end %>
      </h3>

      <% if (blurb = item.blurb(180)).present? %>
        <p class="mt-1.5 line-clamp-3 text-xs leading-relaxed text-soft"><%= blurb %></p>
      <% end %>

      <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-3 gap-y-1 pt-3 text-xs">
        <%= button_to "Unsave", unsave_feed_item_path(item), method: :patch,
              class: "reader-verb", form_class: "contents" %>
        <%= link_to "Task", new_task_path(title: item.title, section_ids: item.feed.section_ids),
              class: "reader-verb" %>
        <% if url %>
          <%= link_to url, class: "reader-verb ml-auto", **ReaderHelper::OUTBOUND do %>
            Open<span aria-hidden="true"> ↗</span>
          <% end %>
        <% end %>
      </div>
    </article>
  <% end %>
</div>
